@HD	VN:1.6	SO:unsorted
@SQ	SN:chr1	LN:1000
@CO	Records for queries/strand/bsbolt.toml
@CO	queries/strand/bsbolt.toml -- YS alone; note 0x10 is inverted on the two _G2A records.
@CO	The FLAGs are the ones BSBolt itself wrote in alnbase-validation/demos/bsbolt-strand: 0x10 and
@CO	0x20 both come from the Crick contig rather than from orientation, so neither is set on
@CO	a Watson record and both are set on a Crick one. 0x2 is absent there only because bwa
@CO	had too few pairs to estimate an insert size, so it is left off here too.
@CO	Each QNAME is the call the rule must make for that record: "<original>:<aligned>",
@CO	each side forward or reverse, or "unknown". Anything after the first "/" is a label
@CO	for the reader. The test that enforces it is in src/strand_rule.rs.
forward:forward/W_C2T	65	chr1	101	60	4M	=	301	200	ACGT	IIII	YS:Z:W_C2T
forward:reverse/W_G2A	129	chr1	101	60	4M	=	301	-200	ACGT	IIII	YS:Z:W_G2A
reverse:reverse/C_C2T	113	chr1	101	60	4M	=	301	-200	ACGT	IIII	YS:Z:C_C2T
reverse:forward/C_G2A	177	chr1	101	60	4M	=	301	200	ACGT	IIII	YS:Z:C_G2A
unknown/WC	4	*	0	0	*	*	0	0	ACGT	IIII	YS:Z:WC
